- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 177\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 25,092 / 300,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'PCA-Combat Embedding with BBKNN Graph' (ID: 299) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.619015964345366\n**ASW_batch:** 0.660\n**ASW_label:** 0.222\n**ARI:** 0.586\n**NMI:** 0.683\n**Graph_conn:** 0.875\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.024\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.360\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.660  ASW_label: 0.222  ARI: 0.586  NMI: 0.683\n\
    \  Graph_conn: 0.875  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.024  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.360\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830784  ASW_label: 0.539577  ARI: 0.586255  NMI: 0.683127\n  Graph_conn: 0.877385  kBET: 0.753195  iLISI: 0.023565  cLISI: 0.997499\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.315621\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 299\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing the unavailable BBKNN library with standard nearest neighbor graph construction.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use `sc.external.pp.bbknn()` (Batch Balanced k-Nearest Neighbors) to construct a batch-aware graph, but the `bbknn` package is not installed in the evaluation environment. This caused an `ImportError` with the message: \"Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\"\n\nThe error occurred at line 35 of the original submission:\n```python\nsc.external.pp.bbknn(graph_adata, batch_key='batch')\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the\
    \ code in `submissions/submission_v2.py` to use Scanpy's built-in nearest neighbor graph construction instead of BBKNN:\n\n**Original approach (failed):**\n```python\n# Run BBKNN. It will add 'connectivities' and 'distances' to graph_adata.obsp\nsc.external.pp.bbknn(graph_adata, batch_key='batch')\n```\n\n**Fixed approach (successful):**\n```python\n# Use standard nearest neighbors instead of BBKNN\n# This will add 'connectivities' and 'distances' to graph_adata.obsp\nsc.pp.neighbors(graph_adata, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X')\n```\n\nThe fix maintains the same workflow:\n1. Normalize and log-transform data\n2. Compute PCA with 50 components\n3. Apply Combat to PCA latent space to get corrected embedding\n4. Build a nearest neighbor graph on the corrected embedding (changed from BBKNN to standard neighbors)\n5. Return output with both corrected embedding and graph\n\n## Evaluation Results\nThe fixed code executed successfully and achieved a score of **0.619** on the human dataset.\n\n\
    **Performance Metrics (Normalized 0-1):**\n- **Batch correction:** ASW_batch: 0.660, kBET: 0.789, iLISI: 0.024, Graph_conn: 0.875\n- **Biological preservation:** ASW_label: 0.222, ARI: 0.586, NMI: 0.683, cLISI: 0.991\n- **Other:** PCR: 1.000, Cell_cycle: 0.360\n\nThe code ran without errors and completed the batch integration task as intended. While the score is not as high as might be achieved with the originally intended BBKNN method, the submission now runs successfully in the available environment.\n\n## Execution Details\n- **Status:** Completed\n- **Success:** True\n- **Score:** 0.619015964345366\n- **Submission Version:** v2\n- **No crashes or errors in execution**\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Combines PCA-Combat embedding with a nearest neighbor graph.\n    Modified to use standard neighbors instead of BBKNN (which is not installed).\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Hybrid PCA-Combat + NN Graph method...\")\n\n    # === Step 1: Generate the corrected embedding (SOTA from ID 292) ===\n    print(\"  Normalizing and logging data...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    print(\"  Computing PCA with 50 components...\")\n    n_pcs = 50\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=False)  # Use all genes for PCA\n\n    # Create a temporary AnnData for Combat\n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata.obs)\n\n    print(\"  Applying Combat to PCA latent space...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n\n    # This is our final corrected embedding\n    corrected_embedding = pca_adata.X\n\n    # === Step 2: Build a standard NN graph on the corrected embedding ===\n    # Create a new AnnData\
    \ object to hold the embedding for graph construction\n    graph_adata = ad.AnnData(X=corrected_embedding)\n    graph_adata.obs = adata.obs\n\n    print(\"  Computing nearest neighbor graph on the corrected embedding...\")\n    # Use standard nearest neighbors instead of BBKNN\n    # This will add 'connectivities' and 'distances' to graph_adata.obsp\n    sc.pp.neighbors(graph_adata, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X')\n\n    # === Step 3: Create and return output with BOTH embedding and graph ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'pca_combat_with_nn_graph'\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': corrected_embedding\n        },\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': graph_adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n            'distances': graph_adata.obsp['distances']\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Hybrid method complete. Output\
    \ has embedding and graph.\")\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Hybrid PCA-Combat + NN Graph method...\n  Normalizing and logging data...\n  Computing PCA with 50 components...\n  Applying Combat to PCA latent space...\n  Computing nearest neighbor graph on the corrected embedding...\n✓ Hybrid method complete. Output has embedding and graph.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ce9668d6-b725-47cb-aeb1-42aa08e72ed3/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ce9668d6-b725-47cb-aeb1-42aa08e72ed3\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'PCA-Combat Embedding with BBKNN Graph' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 299.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 299 | 1 | PCA-Combat Embedding with BBKNN Graph | Veritas I | 176 | 0.6190 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.789 |\n| 294 | 1 | kNN Graph on PCA-Combat Embedding | Veritas I | 175 | 0.3160 | 0.586\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.000 |\n| 292 | 1 | PCA-based Combat Correction | Veritas I | 174 | 0.6187 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.786 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
    \ executing actions."
