- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 180\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 34,302 / 300,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'MNN Correction on Gene Expression\
    \ Space (v2 - Fix)' (ID: 304) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6008457907426784\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.593\n**NMI:** 0.694\n**Graph_conn:** 0.877\n**kBET:** 0.612\n**iLISI:** 0.035\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.593  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.877  kBET: 0.612  iLISI: 0.035  cLISI: 0.986\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832852  ASW_label: 0.540219  ARI: 0.593293  NMI: 0.694091\n  Graph_conn: 0.879575  kBET: 0.586550  iLISI: 0.034933  cLISI: 0.995952\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.284672\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 304\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing MNN correction (which requires unavailable `mnnpy` package) with Combat correction (built into scanpy). The fixed submission achieved\
    \ a score of **0.6008** on the batch integration task.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use `sc.external.pp.mnn_correct()` for batch correction, which requires the external `mnnpy` package:\n\n```python\nadata_corrected = sc.external.pp.mnn_correct(*adata_batches, batch_key='batch')[0]\n```\n\nThis resulted in:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mnnpy'\nImportError: Please install the package mnnpy (https://github.com/chriscainx/mnnpy)\n```\n\nThe `mnnpy` package is not available in the evaluation environment (batch_integration conda environment), causing the submission to crash before any batch correction could be performed.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the MNN correction approach with **Combat** batch correction, which is built directly into scanpy and doesn't require external dependencies:\n\n### Key Changes:\n1. **Removed batch splitting logic** - Combat works on the full AnnData object, not individual batches\n2. **Replaced MNN call** with `sc.pp.combat(adata,\
    \ key='batch')`\n3. **Updated method_id** to 'combat_correct_on_genes_v2' for proper tracking\n\n### Code Comparison:\n**Before (v1 - Failed):**\n```python\n# Split by batch\nbatches = adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories\nadata_batches = [adata[adata.obs['batch'] == b] for b in batches]\n\n# MNN correction (requires mnnpy)\nadata_corrected = sc.external.pp.mnn_correct(*adata_batches, batch_key='batch')[0]\n```\n\n**After (v2 - Success):**\n```python\n# Combat correction (built into scanpy)\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n```\n\n## Performance\n- **Execution**: Completed successfully without errors\n- **Score**: 0.6008 (normalized across 10 OpenProblems metrics)\n- **Method**: Combat is a well-established batch correction method that adjusts gene expression using linear models\n- **Reliability**: Combat is more portable since it has no external dependencies beyond scanpy\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent (Veritas I) should be aware that:\n1. **MNN requires mnnpy** - This external package\
    \ may not always be available\n2. **Combat is a reliable alternative** - Built into scanpy, no external dependencies\n3. **Check available libraries** - The research task specification lists available libraries; stick to those\n4. **Combat performance** - Achieved 60% normalized score, which is reasonable for batch integration\n\nThe fix successfully resolves the dependency issue while maintaining the batch correction workflow.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies Combat batch correction to the gene expression data.\n    v2: Uses Combat instead of MNN to avoid mnnpy dependency.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Combat Correction method (v2)...\")\n\n    # 1. Standard normalization\n   \
    \ print(\"  Normalizing and logging data...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Apply Combat correction on the log-normalized data\n    print(\"  Applying Combat correction...\")\n    # Combat works in-place on adata.X\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n    # 3. Compute PCA on the corrected data\n    print(\"  Computing PCA on Combat-corrected data...\")\n    n_pcs = 50\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    # 4. Create and return the output AnnData\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_correct_on_genes_v2'\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_pca']\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Combat Correction (v2) complete. Final embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Combat Correction method (v2)...\n  Normalizing and logging data...\n  Applying Combat correction...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Computing PCA on Combat-corrected data...\n✓ Combat Correction (v2) complete. Final embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e9ee2736-5cdc-43fa-973b-83b68a56cd10/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e9ee2736-5cdc-43fa-973b-83b68a56cd10\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'MNN Correction on Gene Expression Space (v2 - Fix)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 304.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 304 | 1 | MNN Correction on Gene Expression Space (v2 - Fix) | Veritas I | 179 | 0.6008 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.612 |\n| 302 | 1 | MNN Correction on Gene Expression Space | Veritas I | 177 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 299 | 1 | PCA-Combat Embedding with BBKNN Graph | Veritas I | 176 | 0.6190 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.789 |\n| 294 | 1 | kNN Graph on PCA-Combat Embedding | Veritas I | 175 | 0.3160 | 0.586 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.000 |\n| 292 | 1 | PCA-based Combat Correction | Veritas I | 174 | 0.6187 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.786 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 |\
    \ 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
