parts:
- text: "My reflection session is complete. I have successfully generated three novel ideas to build upon the Combat baseline, as required by the Stagnation Protocol:\n1.  **Control Gene-Guided Combat:** Learn batch effects from non-highly-variable genes and apply the correction globally.\n2.  **Locally-Adaptive Combat:** Pre-cluster the data and apply Combat independently to each cluster.\n3.  **Residual Combat:** Protect the main biological signal (top PCs), apply Combat to the remaining residual data, and then recombine them.\n\nI am now on **Step 4: Experiment**. The first part of this step is to reproduce the baseline score. This will validate my experimental setup and provide a direct point of comparison for my new ideas. I will go to the Research Counter and submit the code for the \"Combat Manual Baseline\" (ID 2).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Reproduction: Combat Manual\"\ntags: \"baseline, combat, empirical-bayes, stagnation-protocol\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This submission is a direct reproduction of the 'Combat Manual Baseline' (ID 2) as the first\n  step of the Stagnation Protocol. The goal is to verify the baseline score under my own execution\n  before testing novel ideas. The code is identical to the system's baseline submission.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import stats\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, issparse\n  import warnings\n\n  def _aprior(delta_hat):\n      m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n      s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n      if s2 == 0:\n          s2 = 1e-8\n      return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\n  def _bprior(delta_hat):\n      m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n      s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n      if s2 == 0:\n          s2 = 1e-8\n      return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\n  def _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n      n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n      g_old = g_hat.copy()\n      d_old = d_hat.copy()\n\
    \      change = 1\n      count = 0\n      max_iter = 200\n      while change > conv and count < max_iter:\n          g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n          sum2 = s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1)) @ np.ones((1, s_data.shape[1]))\n          sum2 = sum2**2\n          sum2 = sum2.sum(axis=1)\n          d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n          change = max(\n              (np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(),\n              (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max()\n          )\n          g_old = g_new\n          d_old = d_new\n          count += 1\n      return g_new, d_new\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      if issparse(adata.X):\n          data = adata.X.toarray()\n      else:\n          data = adata.X.copy()\n      data = data.T\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches\
    \ = np.unique(batch_labels)\n      n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n      n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n      batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n      batch_info = []\n      for i, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n          batch_mask = batch_labels == batch\n          batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n          batch_design[batch_indices, i] = 1\n          batch_info.append(batch_indices)\n      n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in batch_info])\n      B_hat = np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)\n      B_hat = np.linalg.inv(B_hat)\n      B_hat = np.dot(B_hat, batch_design.T)\n      grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      batch_means = np.dot(B_hat, data.T).T\n      var_pooled = np.zeros(n_genes)\n      for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n          batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n          batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n          diff = batch_data - batch_mean\n          var_pooled += np.sum(diff**2,\
    \ axis=1)\n      var_pooled = var_pooled / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n      stand_mean = np.dot(grand_mean, np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n      s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n      for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n          batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n          batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n          s_data[:, batch_indices] = (batch_data - batch_mean) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      gamma_hat = np.dot(np.linalg.inv(np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)),\n                        np.dot(batch_design.T, s_data.T)).T\n      delta_hat = []\n      for batch_indices in batch_info:\n          batch_var = np.var(s_data[:, batch_indices], axis=1, ddof=1)\n          delta_hat.append(batch_var)\n      gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n      t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n      a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n      b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n      gamma_star = []\n      delta_star = []\n      for i, batch_indices in\
    \ enumerate(batch_info):\n          gamma, delta = _it_sol(\n              s_data[:, batch_indices],\n              gamma_hat[:, i],\n              delta_hat[i],\n              gamma_bar,\n              t2,\n              a_prior[i],\n              b_prior[i]\n          )\n          gamma_star.append(gamma)\n          delta_star.append(delta)\n      gamma_star = np.array(gamma_star).T\n      delta_star = np.array(delta_star).T\n      bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n      for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n          dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j])\n          dsq = dsq.reshape((len(dsq), 1))\n          denom = np.dot(dsq, np.ones((1, n_batches[j])))\n          batch_gamma = gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)\n          numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - batch_gamma @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j]))\n          bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / denom\n      vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape((len(var_pooled), 1))\n      bayesdata = bayesdata * np.dot(vpsq, np.ones((1, n_samples)))\
    \ + stand_mean\n      X_corrected = bayesdata.T\n      X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n      temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n      temp_adata.obs_names = adata.obs_names\n      temp_adata.var_names = adata.var_names\n      n_pcs = min(50, temp_adata.n_vars - 1, temp_adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']}\n      )\n      return output\n```"
thinking_content: '**Focus: Baseline Reproduction and the Next Experiment**


  Okay, I''m back on track with the Stagnation Protocol.  The user wants me to stay the course, and that means diving into the experiments.  First things first, though: I need to reproduce the baseline performance.  I skipped the literature review, as I''m still figuring things out, but the baseline selection is done (Combat Manual Baseline, ID 2), and the initial reflection helped clarify three distinct ideas: control gene-guided combat, locally-adaptive combat via pre-clustering, and residual combat on a PCA-reconstructed biological subspace.


  Now it''s experiment time.  The protocol demands a faithful reproduction of the baseline score before any of those shiny new ideas get a look-in.  So, I''m heading to the Research Counter.  I''ll pull the code for the "Combat Manual Baseline" (ID 2), the same one I reviewed earlier at tick 174.  I have the code saved. I''ll execute the script `/execute_action{submit 1}` using that exact code. This is my control experiment. Reproducing the baseline will tell me if I''m even *capable* of executing the basic instructions, and sets my personal benchmark for the next phases.

  '
