parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 201\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,623 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Idea 1: Control Gene-Guided Combat' (ID: 354) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.22358661077750583\n**ASW_batch:** 1.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.153\n**ARI:** 0.000\n**NMI:** 0.012\n**Graph_conn:** 0.116\n**kBET:** 0.301\n**iLISI:** 0.553\n**cLISI:** 0.102\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 1.000  ASW_label: 0.153  ARI: 0.000  NMI: 0.012\n  Graph_conn: 0.116  kBET: 0.301  iLISI: 0.553  cLISI: 0.102\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores\
    \ (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 1.000000  ASW_label: 0.500000  ARI: 0.000035  NMI: 0.012101\n  Graph_conn: 0.130842  kBET: 0.293869  iLISI: 0.552569  cLISI: 0.738316\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: nan\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 354\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the array shape error by properly handling batches with different sample sizes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical error when creating standardized data arrays for batch correction:\n\n```python\ns_data_ctrl = np.array([(control_data[:, indices] - batch_means_ctrl[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_ctrl[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8) for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info)])\n```\n\nThis line attempted to create a NumPy array from a list comprehension where each element corresponds to a different batch. The problem: **each batch has a different number of samples**, resulting in arrays of different shapes along axis 1. NumPy cannot create a homogeneous array from such inhomogeneous\
    \ data, leading to:\n\n```\nValueError: setting an array element with a sequence. The requested array has an inhomogeneous shape after 2 dimensions. The detected shape was (4, 512) + inhomogeneous part.\n```\n\nThe same issue existed in the code for `s_data_full` (line 88 of the original submission).\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the approach from trying to create a single array from the list comprehension to:\n\n1. **Create a list of standardized arrays** (one per batch)\n2. **Concatenate them along axis 1** (samples dimension)\n\n**For control genes:**\n```python\n# Original (broken):\ns_data_ctrl = np.array([(control_data[:, indices] - batch_means_ctrl[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_ctrl[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8) for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info)])\ns_data_ctrl = np.concatenate(s_data_ctrl, axis=1)\n\n# Fixed:\ns_data_ctrl_list = []\nfor i, indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n    standardized = (control_data[:, indices] - batch_means_ctrl[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_ctrl[:,\
    \ np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    s_data_ctrl_list.append(standardized)\ns_data_ctrl = np.concatenate(s_data_ctrl_list, axis=1)\n```\n\n**For all genes:**\n```python\n# Original (broken):\ns_data_full = np.array([(data[:, indices] - batch_means_full[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_full[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8) for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info)])\ns_data_full = np.concatenate(s_data_full, axis=1)\n\n# Fixed:\ns_data_full_list = []\nfor i, indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n    standardized = (data[:, indices] - batch_means_full[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_full[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    s_data_full_list.append(standardized)\ns_data_full = np.concatenate(s_data_full_list, axis=1)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix is working correctly. The code is executing the batch correction algorithm as intended.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The original code had\
    \ a redundant `np.concatenate()` call after the broken `np.array()` call, suggesting the author understood that concatenation was needed but applied it in the wrong order\n- The fix maintains the exact same logic and mathematical operations, just restructures the code to avoid the shape incompatibility\n- This is a common pitfall when working with variable-length sequences in NumPy\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n# Helper functions from the baseline Combat implementation\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n\
    \    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old = g_hat.copy()\n    d_old = d_hat.copy()\n    change = 1\n    count = 0\n    max_iter = 200\n    while change > conv and count < max_iter:\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n        sum2 = (s_data - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2\n        sum2 = sum2.sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        change = max(\n            (np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(),\n            (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max()\n        )\n        g_old, d_old, count = g_new, d_new, count + 1\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # 1. Normalization\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Identify control genes (non-HVGs)\n    # The task provides\
    \ HVGs in adata.var['batch_hvg']\n    control_gene_mask = ~adata.var['batch_hvg'].values\n\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    control_data = data[control_gene_mask, :]\n\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches, n_samples = np.unique(batch_labels), data.shape[1]\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_design = np.array(sc.get.obs_df(adata, keys=['batch']).iloc[:, 0].astype('category').cat.codes.values)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches_total)[batch_design]\n\n    batch_info = [np.where(batch_labels == b)[0] for b in unique_batches]\n    n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in batch_info])\n\n    # 3. Estimate batch parameters using ONLY control genes\n    print(f\"Estimating batch effects from {control_data.shape[0]} control genes...\")\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T\n    grand_mean_ctrl = np.mean(control_data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means_ctrl\
    \ = B_hat @ control_data.T\n\n    var_pooled_ctrl = np.sum([((control_data[:, indices] - batch_means_ctrl[i, :][:, np.newaxis])**2).sum(axis=1) for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info)], axis=0) / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    stand_mean_ctrl = grand_mean_ctrl @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n\n    # FIX: Instead of trying to create a single array from different-sized batches,\n    # concatenate them properly\n    s_data_ctrl_list = []\n    for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        standardized = (control_data[:, indices] - batch_means_ctrl[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_ctrl[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n        s_data_ctrl_list.append(standardized)\n    s_data_ctrl = np.concatenate(s_data_ctrl_list, axis=1)\n\n    gamma_hat = (np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T @ s_data_ctrl.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data_ctrl[:, indices], axis=1, ddof=1) for indices in batch_info]\n\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat,\
    \ axis=1, ddof=1)\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\n    gamma_star_ctrl, delta_star_ctrl = [], []\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        gamma, delta = _it_sol(s_data_ctrl[:, batch_indices], gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i], gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[i], b_prior[i])\n        gamma_star_ctrl.append(gamma)\n        delta_star_ctrl.append(delta)\n\n    gamma_star = np.array(gamma_star_ctrl).T\n    delta_star = np.array(delta_star_ctrl).T\n\n    # 4. Apply correction learned from control genes to ALL genes\n    print(\"Applying learned correction to all genes...\")\n    grand_mean_full = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means_full = B_hat @ data.T\n    var_pooled_full = np.sum([((data[:, indices] - batch_means_full[i, :][:, np.newaxis])**2).sum(axis=1) for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info)], axis=0) / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    stand_mean_full = grand_mean_full @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n\
    \n    # FIX: Same fix here - concatenate properly instead of creating inhomogeneous array\n    s_data_full_list = []\n    for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        standardized = (data[:, indices] - batch_means_full[i, :][:, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled_full[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n        s_data_full_list.append(standardized)\n    s_data_full = np.concatenate(s_data_full_list, axis=1)\n\n    bayesdata = s_data_full.copy()\n    for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        # We need to broadcast the control-gene parameters to all genes\n        gamma_star_broadcast = np.mean(gamma_star, axis=0) # Simple averaging to get per-batch effects\n        delta_star_broadcast = np.mean(delta_star, axis=0)\n\n        denom = np.sqrt(delta_star_broadcast[j])\n        numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - gamma_star_broadcast[j]\n        bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / denom\n\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled_full).reshape((-1, 1))\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * vpsq + stand_mean_full\n\
    \n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T)\n\n    # 5. Final Embedding\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=50)\n\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']})\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nEstimating batch effects from 512 control genes...\nApplying learned correction to all genes...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/48f5faee-2224-4719-890a-ac0904dd8ebe/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 48f5faee-2224-4719-890a-ac0904dd8ebe\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmp8h0win2n/submission.py:28: RuntimeWarning: invalid value\
    \ encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/sklearn/decomposition/_pca.py:787: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  self.explained_variance_ratio_ = self.explained_variance_ / total_var\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET\
