- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 203\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 100,127 / 300,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Idea 2: Locally-Adaptive Combat' (ID: 358) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.35955977235406766\n**ASW_batch:** 0.339\n**ASW_label:** 0.087\n**ARI:** 0.207\n**NMI:** 0.455\n**Graph_conn:** 0.728\n**kBET:** 0.701\n**iLISI:** 0.113\n**cLISI:** 0.736\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.229\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.339  ASW_label: 0.087  ARI: 0.207  NMI: 0.455\n  Graph_conn: 0.728  kBET: 0.701  iLISI: 0.113  cLISI: 0.736\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.229\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.686298  ASW_label: 0.461881  ARI: 0.206857  NMI: 0.455188\n  Graph_conn: 0.732595  kBET: 0.669692  iLISI: 0.113114  cLISI: 0.923148\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.204639\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 358\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission and achieved a score of 0.360\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an issue in how it created the output AnnData object. The problem was in these lines:\n\n```python\noutput = ad.AnnData(\n    obs=adata.obs[[]],  # WRONG: Creates DataFrame with correct indices but NO columns\n    var=adata.var[[]],  # WRONG: Creates DataFrame with correct indices but NO columns\n    obsm={'X_emb': adata_final.obsm['X_pca']}\n)\n```\n\nThe syntax `adata.obs[[]]` creates a DataFrame with all the rows (correct indices) but zero columns. While this preserves the index, it can cause issues when AnnData tries to determine the shape of the object, especially when `X` is not provided.\n\nAdditionally,\
    \ the original code didn't handle potential NaN or Inf values that could arise from Combat's processing of genes with zero variance.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### 1. Fixed Output AnnData Creation\nChanged from empty column DataFrames to full copies:\n\n```python\noutput = ad.AnnData(\n    X=None,  # Explicitly set to None (only embedding needed)\n    obs=adata.obs.copy(),  # Keep full obs DataFrame with all columns\n    var=adata.var.copy(),  # Keep full var DataFrame with all columns\n    obsm={'X_emb': pca_result}\n)\n```\n\n### 2. Added NaN/Inf Handling\nAdded validation and cleaning before PCA:\n\n```python\nif np.isnan(X_corrected_full).any() or np.isinf(X_corrected_full).any():\n    print(f\"  WARNING: Found NaN or Inf values in corrected data!\")\n    X_corrected_full = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected_full, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n    adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n```\n\n### 3. Fixed Matrix Conversion Inconsistency\nEnsured consistent\
    \ array conversion when assigning Combat results:\n\n```python\nif hasattr(adata_subset.X, 'toarray'):\n    X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X.toarray()\nelse:\n    X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X\n```\n\n## Result\nThe submission now runs successfully and achieves a score of **0.360** on the batch integration task. The locally-adaptive Combat approach successfully:\n- Processes all 26 clusters\n- Handles clusters with single batches appropriately\n- Generates a valid 50-dimensional PCA embedding\n- Passes all validation checks in the evaluation system\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies Combat in a locally-adaptive manner by pre-clustering\
    \ the data.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Locally-Adaptive Combat method...\")\n\n    # 1. Standard normalization\n    print(\"  Normalizing and logging data...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Pre-clustering on uncorrected data\n    print(\"  Performing pre-clustering...\")\n    # Create a temporary AnnData for clustering\n    adata_uncorrected = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_uncorrected, n_comps=50)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_uncorrected)\n    sc.tl.leiden(adata_uncorrected, resolution=0.5)\n\n    cluster_labels = adata_uncorrected.obs['leiden']\n    unique_clusters = cluster_labels.unique()\n    print(f\"  Found {len(unique_clusters)} clusters.\")\n\n    # 3. Apply Combat cluster by cluster\n    # Create an empty matrix to hold the final corrected data\n    X_corrected_full = np.zeros_like(adata.X.toarray())\n\n    for cluster in unique_clusters:\n        print(f\"    Processing cluster {cluster}...\")\n        cluster_mask\
    \ = (cluster_labels == cluster).values\n\n        # Subset the original AnnData to this cluster\n        adata_subset = adata[cluster_mask, :].copy()\n\n        # Skip clusters with only one batch, as Combat will fail\n        if adata_subset.obs['batch'].nunique() < 2:\n            print(f\"    Skipping cluster {cluster}, only has one batch.\")\n            X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X.toarray()\n            continue\n\n        # Apply Combat to the subset\n        # Using the built-in scanpy function for simplicity and robustness\n        try:\n            sc.pp.combat(adata_subset, key='batch')\n            # FIXED: Always convert to array for consistent assignment\n            if hasattr(adata_subset.X, 'toarray'):\n                X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X.toarray()\n            else:\n                X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X\n        except ValueError as e:\n            # Handle cases where a batch has only\
    \ one cell in the cluster\n            print(f\"    Combat failed for cluster {cluster}: {e}. Using original data.\")\n            X_corrected_full[cluster_mask, :] = adata_subset.X.toarray()\n\n    # 4. Reassemble and perform final PCA\n    print(\"  Reassembling data and performing final PCA...\")\n    adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n\n    # Check for NaN/Inf before PCA\n    if np.isnan(X_corrected_full).any() or np.isinf(X_corrected_full).any():\n        print(f\"  WARNING: Found NaN or Inf values in corrected data!\")\n        print(f\"  NaN count: {np.isnan(X_corrected_full).sum()}\")\n        print(f\"  Inf count: {np.isinf(X_corrected_full).sum()}\")\n        # Replace NaN/Inf with zeros\n        X_corrected_full = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected_full, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n        adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_final, n_comps=50)\n\n    # Verify PCA output\n  \
    \  pca_result = adata_final.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"  PCA output shape: {pca_result.shape}\")\n    print(f\"  PCA has NaN: {np.isnan(pca_result).any()}\")\n    print(f\"  PCA has Inf: {np.isinf(pca_result).any()}\")\n\n    # 5. Create and return output\n    # CRITICAL: Keep the original obs/var structure with correct indices\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        X=None,  # No X matrix needed\n        obs=adata.obs.copy(),  # Keep full obs DataFrame\n        var=adata.var.copy(),  # Keep full var DataFrame\n        obsm={'X_emb': pca_result}\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ Locally-Adaptive Combat complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Locally-Adaptive Combat method...\n  Normalizing and logging data...\n\
