parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 221\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 169,303 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's EtC + Praxis I's BRBG' (ID: 392) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.62391782208538\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.615\n**NMI:** 0.693\n**Graph_conn:** 0.878\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.034\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.615  NMI: 0.693\n  Graph_conn: 0.878  kBET: 0.780  iLISI: 0.034  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores\
    \ (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.614690  NMI: 0.693531\n  Graph_conn: 0.880312  kBET: 0.744318  iLISI: 0.034323  cLISI: 0.996133\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 392\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code and achieved a score of 0.624. The submission now runs without crashing and successfully implements the SOTA replication combining Daedalus II's Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with Praxis I's Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph (BRBG).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect usage of the `scanpy.Neighbors` API in the `_build_balanced_knn_equal` function. The code was attempting to use an outdated or incorrect API pattern with parameters that don't exist:\n\n1. **First error (v1)**: Used `k=` parameter instead of `n_neighbors=`\n2. **Second error (v2)**: Used `X_ext=` parameter which doesn't exist in `compute_neighbors()`\n\nThe function was trying to use a low-level `Neighbors`\
    \ object with non-existent parameters, when the correct approach is to use the high-level `sc.pp.neighbors()` function.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version v3** - Rewrote the `_build_balanced_knn_equal` function to use the correct scanpy API:\n\n### Original problematic code:\n```python\nnn = sc.Neighbors(adata=ad.AnnData(X=Z))\nnn.compute_neighbors(k=k_per_batch, X_ext=Z_batch, metric=metric)\nD_list.append(nn.distances)\nC_list.append(nn.connectivities)\n```\n\n### Fixed code:\n```python\n# Create AnnData with full dataset\nadata_full = ad.AnnData(X=Z)\n\n# Compute neighbors using the high-level API\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata_full, n_neighbors=k_per_batch, metric=metric)\n\n# Extract the subset corresponding to batch cells\nbatch_indices = np.where(mask)[0]\nC_batch = adata_full.obsp['connectivities'][batch_indices, :]\nD_batch = adata_full.obsp['distances'][batch_indices, :]\n```\n\n### Key changes:\n1. **Use `sc.pp.neighbors()`** instead of low-level `Neighbors` class - this is the recommended\
    \ scanpy API\n2. **Compute neighbors on full dataset** then extract the relevant rows for each batch\n3. **Extract batch-specific subsets** using boolean indexing with `np.where(mask)[0]`\n4. **Use `vstack`** instead of `hstack` to properly concatenate the sparse matrices vertically (one row per cell)\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Completed successfully\n- **Score**: 0.624\n- **Versions created**: v2 (failed), v3 (succeeded)\n- **Final submission**: submissions/submission_v3.py\n\nThe code now correctly implements the balanced k-NN graph construction with batch-aware neighbor selection, completing the SOTA replication pipeline.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# --- BRBG Helper Functions\
    \ (from Praxis I's storage) ---\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    unique_batches, batch_indices = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    one_hot = np.eye(len(unique_batches), dtype=np.float32)[batch_indices]\n    return one_hot, unique_batches\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, solver='auto')\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    R2 = 1 - np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0) / np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    return Z_hat, R2\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total, metric):\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    k_per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / n_batches))\n\n    D_list, C_list = [], []\n    for b in unique_batches:\n        mask = batches == b\n        Z_batch = Z[mask, :]\n\n        # FIX: Create AnnData with the batch data and compute neighbors on it\n        # Then we need to find neighbors in the full dataset Z\n        adata_full\
    \ = ad.AnnData(X=Z)\n        adata_batch = ad.AnnData(X=Z_batch)\n\n        # Compute neighbors: for each cell in Z_batch, find k_per_batch neighbors in Z\n        sc.pp.neighbors(adata_full, n_neighbors=k_per_batch, metric=metric)\n\n        # Extract the subset corresponding to batch cells\n        batch_indices = np.where(mask)[0]\n        C_batch = adata_full.obsp['connectivities'][batch_indices, :]\n        D_batch = adata_full.obsp['distances'][batch_indices, :]\n\n        D_list.append(D_batch)\n        C_list.append(C_batch)\n\n    D = sp.vstack(D_list, format='csr')\n    C = sp.vstack(C_list, format='csr')\n    return C, D\n\n# --- Main Function ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting SOTA Replication: EtC + BRBG...\")\n    adata_orig = adata.copy() # Keep original for graph path\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH (Daedalus II's EtC) ---\n    print(\"  Generating EtC embedding...\")\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n\n    adata_hvg = adata_emb[:, adata_emb.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=60)\n\n    # ComBat on PCs\n    pca_data = ad.AnnData(X=adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_hvg.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_data, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_data.X\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH (Praxis I's BRBG) ---\n    print(\"  Generating BRBG graph...\")\n    adata_graph = adata_orig.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n\n    adata_hvg_graph = adata_graph[:, adata_graph.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg_graph, n_comps=50)\n    Zg = adata_hvg_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\
    \    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(0.74, 0.9 * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n\n    # --- COMBINE AND OUTPUT ---\n    print(\"  Combining outputs...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs.copy(),\n        var=adata.var.copy(),\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb},\n        obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ SOTA Replication complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting SOTA Replication: EtC + BRBG...\n  Generating EtC embedding...\n  Generating BRBG graph...\n  Combining outputs...\n✓ SOTA Replication complete.\n\
    \  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/2bfb2479-bcf8-43df-bc4a-bd301a158e99/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 2bfb2479-bcf8-43df-bc4a-bd301a158e99\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 397 | 1 | Sophia\
    \ II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05) | Sophia II | 221 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 396 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Soft-Whiten Embedding (tau=0.95): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Whitening | Praxis I | 221 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 395 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA64 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 221 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 394 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors | Daedalus II | 220 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 393 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=45) | Praxis I | 220 | 0.7327 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 392 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's EtC + Praxis I's BRBG | Veritas I | 219 | 0.6239 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.780 |\n| 391 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph\
