tick: 223
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 223\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 175,695 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 57 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 391**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph\n**ID:** 391\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, pca, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine\n**Abstract:** Embedding path: normalize/log1p → HVGs → PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores to form X_emb (EtC). Graph path: residualized PCA50 on HVGs with adaptive gamma and equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary). Tests the inverted pipeline with our standard BRBG graph.\n**Score:** 0.732755189030825\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:**\
    \ 0.744\n**NMI:** 0.703\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.781\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.744  NMI: 0.703\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.781  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.743686  NMI: 0.703064\n  Graph_conn: 0.946639  kBET: 0.745612  iLISI: 0.935294  cLISI: 0.990319\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n\
    \    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b\
    \ in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: \n            continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: \n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d\
    \ in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding path: PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PCs (EtC)\n    ad_emb = adata.copy()\n    ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']  # (n, 60)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')  # ComBat in PC space\n    X_emb = ad_pc.X\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: PCA50 on HVGs → adaptive residualization → balanced kNN\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\
    \    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/6b1fe390-1ab9-40ef-9557-bf4326d6624d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 6b1fe390-1ab9-40ef-9557-bf4326d6624d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 391` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 391 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1\
    \ | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 400 | 1 | Analysis: Biological Signal Preservation in PC vs Gene Space | Daedalus II | 223 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 399 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (gamma_max=0.75) | Praxis I | 223 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 398 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors (v2) | Daedalus II | 222 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 397 | 1 | Sophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05) | Sophia II | 221 | 0.4534 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.052 | 0.972 | 0.700\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.167 |\n| 396 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Soft-Whiten Embedding (tau=0.95): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Whitening | Praxis I | 221 | 0.7148 | 0.744 | 0.837 | 0.168 | 0.107 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.742 |\n| 395 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA64 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 221 | 0.7320 | 0.744 | 0.690 | 0.216 | 0.351 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.768 |\n| 394 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors | Daedalus II | 220 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 393 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=45) | Praxis I | 220 | 0.7327 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 392 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's EtC + Praxis I's BRBG | Veritas I | 219 | 0.6239 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.780 |\n| 391 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced\
    \ Graph | Praxis I | 219 | 0.7328 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
