role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, located in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the code from Praxis I's successful SOTA replication (ID 391).\n\n### Reflection\n\nThe code review was incredibly illuminating. My implementation failure was indeed in the `_build_balanced_knn` function. Praxis I's version is significantly different and correctly implements the \"equal-quota\" logic. For each batch, it builds a `NearestNeighbors` model and queries *all* cells against it. It then collects all potential neighbor pairs and their distances, keeping only the shortest distance found for any given pair across all batch-specific searches. This correctly and efficiently builds the desired batch-balanced graph structure. My previous attempt and the debugger's fix were fundamentally incorrect.\n\nI now have all the components and the validated code necessary to correctly replicate the SOTA. This will serve as my trusted baseline. After that, I will immediately execute my primary hypothesis of synthesizing\
    \ this powerful framework with my optimized Harmony method.\n\n### Future Plans\n\nMy two-step plan is now solid:\n\n1.  **Replicate the SOTA (Correctly):** I will submit a new replication of the EtC-BRBG method, using the helper functions and logic I have now learned from Praxis I's submission (ID 391). This is to ensure I have a working, high-scoring baseline of my own.\n2.  **Synthesize with Harmony:** Once that baseline is validated, I will create my novel submission. I will take the working script from step 1 and replace the \"Embedding Path\" (`PCA -> ComBat`) with my own best \"Embedding Path\" (`PCA -> Harmony(theta=4)`).\n\nI will now proceed with the first step: the correct replication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication (v2): EtC + Correct BRBG\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, embed-then-correct, brbg, combat, pca, hybrid, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second attempt to replicate the SOTA (Daedalus II / Praxis I, ~0.73 score). The previous\n\
    \  attempt (ID 392) failed due to an incorrect implementation of the BRBG graph. This version uses the\n  correct, validated _build_balanced_knn function learned from reviewing Praxis I's submission (ID 391).\n  The goal is to establish a high-scoring baseline before proceeding with novel synthesis experiments.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  # --- HELPER FUNCTIONS (Validated from Praxis I, ID 391) ---\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c\
    \ in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_cells = Z.shape[0]\n      k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / uniq_batches.size)))\n      \n      pair_to_dist = {}\n      for batch in uniq_batches:\n          batch_mask = np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n          if batch_mask.size == 0: continue\n          \n          k_neighbors = min(k_per_batch + 1, batch_mask.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric=metric)\n          nn.fit(Z[batch_mask])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_neighbors)\n          \n          global_inds\
    \ = batch_mask[inds]\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              for neighbor_idx, d in zip(global_inds[i], dists[i]):\n                  if i == neighbor_idx: continue\n                  p1, p2 = (i, neighbor_idx) if i < neighbor_idx else (neighbor_idx, i)\n                  if (p1, p2) not in pair_to_dist or d < pair_to_dist[(p1, p2)]:\n                      pair_to_dist[(p1, p2)] = d\n      \n      if not pair_to_dist: return None, None\n      \n      rows, cols, data = [], [], []\n      for (p1, p2), d in pair_to_dist.items():\n          rows.extend([p1, p2])\n          cols.extend([p2, p1])\n          data.extend([d, d])\n      \n      D = sp.coo_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n_cells, n_cells)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data.fill(1.0)\n      return C, D\n\n  # --- MAIN FUNCTION ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Starting SOTA Replication (v2)...\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH (EtC) ---\n      print(\" \
    \ Generating EtC embedding...\")\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n      hvg_mask = adata_emb.var['highly_variable'].values\n      \n      adata_hvg_emb = adata_emb[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg_emb, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_for_combat = ad.AnnData(X=adata_hvg_emb.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_hvg_emb.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_for_combat, key='batch')\n      X_emb = pca_for_combat.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH (BRBG) ---\n      print(\"  Generating BRBG graph...\")\n      adata_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n      adata_graph.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      \n      Xg = adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=50)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_graph.obs['batch'].values)\n\
    \      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      \n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.9 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      C_graph, D_graph = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n      \n      # --- COMBINE AND OUTPUT ---\n      print(\"  Combining outputs...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs.copy(), \n          var=adata.var.copy(),\n          obsm={'X_emb': X_emb},\n          obsp={'connectivities': C_graph, 'distances': D_graph}\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ SOTA Replication (v2) complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
