parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 226\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 187,629 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read praxis/brbg_common.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/brbg_common.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 406 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment A - Baseline Replication (Veritas I: PCA-based Combat Correction) | Sophia II | 226 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 405 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + PBVE-Emb (alpha=0.3): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Per-Batch Variance Equalization | Praxis I | 226 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 404 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs + Residualized Graph (lam=1.0, gamma_max=0.74) | Praxis I | 225 | 0.7326 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 403 | 1 | Analysis: Unsupervised Cluster Purity in PC vs Gene Space | Daedalus II | 224 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  | \
    \ |  |  |  |\n| 402 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + BRBG using dataset batch_hvg | Praxis I | 224 | 0.7266 | 0.740 | 0.705 | 0.218 | 0.302 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.754 |\n| 401 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v2): EtC + Correct BRBG | Veritas I | 223 | 0.6240 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.781 |\n| 400 | 1 | Analysis: Biological Signal Preservation in PC vs Gene Space | Daedalus II | 223 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 399 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (gamma_max=0.75) | Praxis I | 223 | 0.7326 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.779 |\n| 398 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors (v2) | Daedalus II | 222 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 397 | 1 | Sophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05) | Sophia II | 221 | 0.4534 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.052 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 0.000\
    \ | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.167 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config (EID 185-like adaptive residualization)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n\
    \    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n\n    # Graph path: PCs on HVGs + adaptive residualization\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec  # broadcast over columns\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding path: ComBat + PCA on HVGs\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n\
    \    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'hvg': 'Seurat v3, batch-aware'\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/brbg_common.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom\
    \ sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(cats)\n    n = cats.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n    col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n    for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n        B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    K\
    \ = B.shape[1]\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n    Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n    # per-PC R^2\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n    return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n# Existing equal-quotas (ceil) builder (kept for compatibility)\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 for potential self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n\
    \        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# Existing min-quota + global fill (kept)\ndef _build_balanced_knn_minq(Z,\
    \ batches, k_total=48, min_per_batch=2, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(min_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:min_per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:min_per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n        \
    \        if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    fill_each = max(0, k_total - int(min_per_batch * uniq.shape[0]))\n    if fill_each > 0:\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z)\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), return_distance=True)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = inds[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:fill_each]\n            di = di[mask][:fill_each]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n\
    \        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# New: exact balanced quotas (q per batch + r extras per node), rotating extras across batches per node\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal_exact(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = uniq.shape[0]\n    if B == 0 or k_total <= 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    q = k_total // B\n    r = k_total % B\n\n    # Pre-fit per-batch NNs up to max needed neighbors (q + 1 extra + self)\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for bi, b in enumerate(uniq):\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        kmax = min(q + 1 + 1, idx_train.size)  # q + possible extra + self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kmax, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=kmax, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Rotate extras for fairness: r batches get +1 neighbor for node i\n            order = [(bi + i) % B for bi in range(B)]\n            extras = set(order[:r])\n            # select k_b for this batch index\n            k_b = q + (1 if bi in extras else 0)\n\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [],\
    \ []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
