role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, in the Research Counter. My previous turn was dedicated to analyzing my failed SOTA replication. I have now read both `best_dual_brbg_adapt.py` and its dependency, `brbg_common.py`, from Praxis I's lineage storage.\n\n### Reflection\n\nMy analysis was correct. I have identified the precise, validated code for the BRBG graph. The helper functions in `brbg_common.py` and the main pipeline in `best_dual_brbg_adapt.py` provide a complete and reproducible implementation. My previous failures were due to subtle but critical errors in my manual transcription and understanding of the `_build_balanced_knn` logic. To eliminate any possibility of error, I will now save a complete, self-contained version of the SOTA pipeline to my own storage. This will serve as a verified tool that I can import and use reliably.\n\n### Future Plans\n\nMy plan is now purely execution-focused.\n\n1.  **Write SOTA to Storage:** I will combine the necessary functions from `brbg_common.py` and the\
    \ `EtC` logic into a single, self-contained script. I will then write this script to my lineage storage at `veritas/sota_pipeline.py`.\n2.  **Submit SOTA Replication (v3):** I will submit a simple wrapper script that imports and runs the function from my new `sota_pipeline.py` file. This should finally achieve the ~0.73 score and validate my baseline.\n3.  **Synthesize with Harmony:** Once the replication is successful, I will modify my stored `sota_pipeline.py` to replace the ComBat embedding path with my Harmony embedding path, and submit that as my novel contribution.\n\nI will now write the consolidated SOTA script to my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write veritas/sota_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  # --- HELPER FUNCTIONS (Consolidated\
    \ from Praxis I) ---\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      return Zhat, R2\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n\
    \      uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_cells = Z.shape[0]\n      k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / uniq_batches.size)))\n      \n      pair_to_dist = {}\n      for batch in uniq_batches:\n          batch_mask = np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n          if batch_mask.size == 0: continue\n          \n          k_neighbors = min(k_per_batch + 1, batch_mask.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric=metric)\n          nn.fit(Z[batch_mask])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_neighbors)\n          \n          global_inds = batch_mask[inds]\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              for neighbor_idx, d in zip(global_inds[i], dists[i]):\n                  if i == neighbor_idx: continue\n                  p1, p2 = (i, neighbor_idx) if i < neighbor_idx else (neighbor_idx, i)\n                  if (p1, p2) not in pair_to_dist or d < pair_to_dist[(p1, p2)]:\n                      pair_to_dist[(p1, p2)] = d\n      \n    \
    \  if not pair_to_dist: return None, None\n      \n      rows, cols, data = [], [], []\n      for (p1, p2), d in pair_to_dist.items():\n          rows.extend([p1, p2]); cols.extend([p2, p1]); data.extend([d, d])\n      \n      D = sp.coo_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n_cells, n_cells)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data.fill(1.0)\n      return C, D\n\n  # --- Main SOTA Pipeline Function ---\n  def sota_replication_pipeline(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n      hvg_mask = adata.var['highly_variable'].values\n      \n      # EMBEDDING (EtC)\n      adata_hvg_emb = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg_emb, n_comps=60)\n      pca_for_combat = ad.AnnData(X=adata_hvg_emb.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_hvg_emb.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_for_combat, key='batch')\n      X_emb = pca_for_combat.X\n \
    \     \n      # GRAPH (BRBG)\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=50)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.9 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      C_graph, D_graph = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n      \n      # OUTPUT\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.copy(),\n                          obsm={'X_emb': X_emb}, obsp={'connectivities': C_graph, 'distances': D_graph})\n      return output\n```"
