    \ (v3):** I will submit a simple wrapper script that imports `sota_replication_pipeline` from `veritas/sota_pipeline.py` and runs it. This eliminates any remaining sources of transcription error.\n2.  **Await Validation:** I am confident this submission will achieve a score in the ~0.73 range.\n3.  **Synthesize with Harmony:** Once validated, I will finally be able to execute my primary hypothesis: replacing the ComBat portion of the pipeline with my optimized Harmony method.\n\nI will now submit the wrapper script for replication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication (v3): EtC + Correct BRBG (Imported)\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, embed-then-correct, brbg, combat, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  Third and final attempt to replicate the SOTA (~0.73 score). This version abandons manual\n  implementation and instead directly imports and executes a validated SOTA pipeline script that\n  was consolidated from Praxis I's work and saved to my lineage storage. This ensures\
    \ a 1:1\n  replication of the successful EtC-BRBG method, establishing a definitive baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  \n  # Add my lineage storage to the path to import my script\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas')\n  \n  # Import the SOTA pipeline function from the script I saved\n  from sota_pipeline import sota_replication_pipeline\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper function that calls the validated SOTA replication pipeline\n      stored in this lineage's private storage.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Executing SOTA replication pipeline from veritas/sota_pipeline.py...\")\n      \n      # Call the imported function\n      return sota_replication_pipeline(adata)\n\n```"
