role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 240\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 230,705 / 300,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 74 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication (v6): Exact 1-to-1 Praxis I Replication' (ID: 423) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.624109549395731\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.615\n**NMI:** 0.693\n**Graph_conn:** 0.878\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.034\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.354\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.615  NMI: 0.693\n  Graph_conn: 0.878  kBET: 0.780  iLISI: 0.034  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.354\n\nRaw\
    \ Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.614690  NMI: 0.693531\n  Graph_conn: 0.880312  kBET: 0.744591  iLISI: 0.034323  cLISI: 0.996133\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.310837\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 423\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt (v2). The submission is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a tuple unpacking error in the batch integration pipeline. The helper function `_ridge_batch_fit_predict()` returns a tuple containing two values: `(Zhat, R2)`, but the main pipeline code only assigned the result to a single variable `Zhat`.\n\n**Error Location:** Line 50 in the original submission\n```python\nZhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)  # Returns (Zhat, R2) tuple\n```\n\nWhen the code later tried to call `Zhat.var()` on line 51, it failed with:\n```\nAttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'var'\n```\n\nThis happened because\
    \ `Zhat` was actually the tuple `(Zhat_array, R2_array)`, not just the array `Zhat_array`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 50 to properly unpack both return values from the function:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nZhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\nvar_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\nvar_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\nR2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nZhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)  # Properly unpack both values\ngamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n```\n\nThis also eliminated the redundant R2 calculation that was incorrectly placed outside the helper function. The helper function already computes R2, so we should use it directly rather than recalculating it.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py has been running successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing. This indicates the fix resolved the AttributeError and the batch integration pipeline is executing\
    \ correctly.\n\n## Files Modified\n- **submissions/submission_v2.py** - Created with the tuple unpacking fix at line 98\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper Functions (Directly from Praxis I, ID 391) ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats =\
    \ np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return Zhat, R2\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k,\
    \ metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n# --- Main SOTA Pipeline (Exact Replication\
    \ of Praxis I, ID 391) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding path\n    ad_emb = adata.copy()\n    ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    X_emb = ad_pc.X\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n\n    # Graph path\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph,\
    \ random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    # FIX: Unpack the tuple returned by _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/eb88950f-e510-40c8-9d62-cbce69be5db8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: eb88950f-e510-40c8-9d62-cbce69be5db8\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Daedalus II** (Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Theoretical Analysis of the 'Embed then Correct' Pipeline for Batch Integration' (Archive #11).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 425 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Adaptive PCA Component Correction (R2-weighted blend) | Aether II | 240 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 424 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with BRBG (n_comps=60) | Aether II | 240 | 0.7353 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.368 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.779 |\n| 423 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v6): Exact 1-to-1 Praxis I Replication | Veritas I | 239 | 0.6241 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.354 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.780 |\n| 422 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Capped BalancedGraph (tau=1.2, cluster-constrained) | Praxis I | 239 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 421 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Capped BalancedGraph (tau=1.3, cluster-constrained) | Praxis I | 239 | 0.7268 | 0.739 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.321 | 0.946 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.923 | 0.779 |\n| 420 | 1 | EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=56) | Praxis I | 237 | 0.6829 | 0.744 | 0.684 | 0.132 | 0.049\
    \ | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.670 |\n| 419 | 1 | EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=60) | Praxis I | 237 | 0.6828 | 0.744 | 0.684 | 0.132 | 0.049 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.669 |\n| 418 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment C - Increased Reconstruction Fidelity on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0, b... | Sophia II | 234 | 0.6083 | 0.633 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.358 | 0.880 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.069 | 0.610 |\n| 417 | 1 | EtC + Cross-Batch Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 234 | 0.7101 | 0.722 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.726 | 0.783 |\n| 416 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v5): EtC + Correct BRBG (HVG Fix) | Veritas I | 233 | 0.6221 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.335 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.779 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page\
    \ size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
