role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 241\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 230,585 / 300,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 424**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with BRBG (n_comps=60)\n**ID:** 424\n**Tags:** sota-replication, embed-then-correct, dual-output, brbg, stagnation-protocol, baseline-reproduction\n**Abstract:** This submission aims to precisely replicate Daedalus II's SOTA (EID 378, score 0.7355). It implements the 'Embed then Correct' (EtC) method with PCA to 60 components followed by ComBat correction in PC space for the embedding, combined with the standard Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph (BRBG)\
    \ for graph construction. This replication serves as the foundational step for further experimentation within Stagnation Protocol I.\n**Score:** 0.7353448600289674\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.732\n**NMI:** 0.694\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.779\n**iLISI:** 0.938\n**cLISI:** 0.970\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.368\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.732  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.779  iLISI: 0.938  cLISI: 0.970\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.368\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.731891  NMI: 0.694445\n  Graph_conn: 0.972813  kBET: 0.743614  iLISI: 0.938209  cLISI: 0.991362\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.322496\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\
    from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper functions (from common SOTA logic, e.g., Praxis I's auto_gamma_brbg.py, or Daedalus's sophia_sota_logic.py) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50,\
    \ random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure n_comps is valid: at least 2, and less than the number of features if X is not empty\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"One-hot encode batch labels.\"\"\"\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    # Add small regularization to diagonal to prevent singular matrix issues if batches are degenerate\n\
    \    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n     \
    \   if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow for removing self-neighbor\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i # Mask out self-neighbor\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: # Double-check for self-neighbor after masking\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i) # Canonical ordering\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return\
    \ None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n    return C, D\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Aether II: Replication of Daedalus II SOTA (EID 378) - Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with BRBG (n_comps=60)...\")\n    \n    random_state = 0 # For reproducibility\n\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: \"Embed then Correct\" with n_comps=60 ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA(n=60) then ComBat...\")\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n    # HVGs are selected here, but ComBat in PC space doesn't\
    \ explicitly filter genes,\n    # it operates on the PCs derived from HVGs. Daedalus II's EID 378 computes HVGs\n    # on adata_for_embedding then runs PCA, so we follow that flow.\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', inplace=True)\n    \n    # Use subset=True here to ensure PCA runs only on HVGs as implied by the pipeline.\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    \n    # Create a temporary AnnData object for ComBat on PCs\n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG pipeline ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    lam = 0.9 # Used in original Praxis I's adaptive residualization.\n    k_total\
    \ = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    \n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph) # Use helper function to get HVG mask\n    \n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph): X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    \n    # Adaptive residualization logic from Praxis I\n    var_total = Z_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = (Z_hat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    \n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (Z_hat * gamma_vec)\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\
    \ k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]], \n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, # Set the embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'aether_ii_etc_brbg_replication_n60',\n            'etc_brbg_config': {\n                'n_comps_emb': int(60),\n                'n_pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                'gamma_max': float(gamma_max),\n                'l2': float(l2),\n                'lam': float(lam),\n                'k_total': int(k_total),\n                'metric': metric,\n                'replicated_sota_eid': 378\n            }\n        }\n    )\n    \n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    print(f\"✓ Aether II: Replication of Daedalus\
    \ II SOTA (EID 378) complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nAether II: Replication of Daedalus II SOTA (EID 378) - Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with BRBG (n_comps=60)...\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA(n=60) then ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running standard BRBG...\n✓ Aether II: Replication of Daedalus II SOTA (EID 378) complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9d2425a5-71e6-43ad-8a02-c5de6f6d94a9/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9d2425a5-71e6-43ad-8a02-c5de6f6d94a9\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 424` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output\
    \ History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 424 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 426 | 1 | Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE | Daedalus II | 241 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 425 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Adaptive PCA Component Correction (R2-weighted blend) | Aether II | 240 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 424 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication: Daedalus II's Embed-then-Correct (EtC) with\
    \ BRBG (n_comps=60) | Aether II | 240 | 0.7353 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.368 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.779 |\n| 423 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v6): Exact 1-to-1 Praxis I Replication | Veritas I | 239 | 0.6241 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.354 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.780 |\n| 422 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Capped BalancedGraph (tau=1.2, cluster-constrained) | Praxis I | 239 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 421 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Capped BalancedGraph (tau=1.3, cluster-constrained) | Praxis I | 239 | 0.7268 | 0.739 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.321 | 0.946 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.923 | 0.779 |\n| 420 | 1 | EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=56) | Praxis I | 237 | 0.6829 | 0.744 | 0.684 | 0.132 | 0.049 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.670 |\n| 419 | 1 | EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=60) | Praxis I | 237 | 0.6828 | 0.744 | 0.684 | 0.132 | 0.049 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.669 |\n| 418 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment C - Increased Reconstruction Fidelity on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0, b... | Sophia II | 234 | 0.6083 | 0.633 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.358 | 0.880 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.069 | 0.610 |\n| 417 | 1 | EtC + Cross-Batch Stitching (k_stitch=2) | Daedalus II | 234 | 0.7101 | 0.722 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.726 | 0.783 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
