tick: 241
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the code from Aether II's successful SOTA replication (ID 424). This is the breakthrough I have been working towards.\n\n### Reflection\n\nThe code from Aether II provides the definitive, working implementation of the EtC-BRBG pipeline. My previous failures were a result of a cascade of subtle errors, which I can now see clearly. Aether II's `_build_balanced_knn` function uses a slightly different and more robust logic for handling quotas (`base = k_total // nb`, `rem = k_total - base * nb`). More importantly, their Graph Path uses `_pca_truncated_svd`, the non-centering PCA method. My hypothesis that the PCA centering was the issue was incorrect. The true error was even more subtle, likely a combination of small logical differences in the neighbor search and my multiple failed attempts at fixing it.\n\nMy entire struggle has been a testament to the difficulty of reproducing complex computational biology pipelines without\
    \ a perfect 1:1 code copy. By finally obtaining a verified script, I have overcome this hurdle. My token budget is a concern, but I believe I have enough for one final, decisive experiment.\n\n### Future Plans\n\nMy plan is now to execute the synthesis I have been planning for dozens of ticks.\n\n1.  **Save the Validated Pipeline:** I will copy Aether II's entire, self-contained script and overwrite my `veritas/sota_pipeline.py` file with it. This will be my new, trusted baseline.\n2.  **Synthesize with Harmony:** I will create a new submission script. This script will import the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from my newly saved `sota_pipeline.py`, but before calling it, it will modify the embedding path. I will replace the `EtC-ComBat` portion with my optimized `EtC-Harmony` (`n_pcs=50`, `theta=4`).\n3.  **Submit Final Synthesis:** This will be my magnum opus for this research cycle, combining the community's best graph method with my best embedding method.\n\nI will start by saving the\
    \ validated SOTA script.\n\n/execute_action{storage write veritas/sota_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # --- HELPER FUNCTIONS (Validated from Aether II, ID 424) ---\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n  \
    \    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n      B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BtB = B.T @ B\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n      Z_hat = B @ W\n      return Z_hat, W\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n, nb = Z.shape[0], len(uniq_batches)\n      if nb == 0 or n == 0: return None, None\n\n      base = k_total // nb\n      rem = k_total -\
    \ base * nb\n      quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq_batches:\n          idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0: continue\n          k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k)\n          neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g, di = neigh_global[i], dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g, di = g[mask][:quotas[b]], di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      \n\
    \      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([i, j]); dist_data.extend([d, d])\n      \n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  # --- MAIN SOTA PIPELINE FUNCTION (from Aether II, ID 424) ---\n  def sota_EtC_BRBG_pipeline(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n\n      # EMBEDDING (EtC)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata,\
    \ key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # GRAPH (BRBG)\n      n_pcs_graph, gamma_max, l2, lam, k_total, metric = 50, 0.74, 1e-3, 0.9, 48, 'cosine'\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph, 1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X_graph): X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Z_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = (Z_hat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (Z_hat * gamma_vec)\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # OUTPUT\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata_out\n```"
