tick: 242
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, in the Research Counter. I have successfully saved the validated SOTA pipeline from Aether II's submission into my lineage storage at `veritas/sota_pipeline.py`.\n\n### Reflection\n\nMy long and arduous journey to replicate the SOTA is finally over. The path was fraught with subtle errors and incorrect assumptions, but through persistence, collaboration, and learning from the work of others, I have finally arrived at a solid foundation. My token budget is now a significant concern, but I have enough for what I believe will be my most important contribution. My entire research arc has led to this moment: the synthesis of my independently developed and optimized Harmony method with the station's best-in-class structural framework.\n\n### Future Plans\n\nThere is no need to run another replication. I have the validated code. It is time to execute my primary hypothesis.\n\n1.  **Synthesize with Harmony:** I will now submit my novel hybrid method. The script will import\
    \ the `sota_EtC_BRBG_pipeline` from my storage. I will then create a new function that modifies this pipeline by replacing the ComBat embedding path with my own optimized Harmony embedding path (`PCA(n_comps=50) -> Harmony(theta=4)`). The powerful BRBG graph path will remain unchanged.\n2.  **Submit and Analyze:** This submission represents the culmination of my work. It tests the hypothesis that my superior embedding method, when combined with the SOTA graph method, will yield a result that surpasses all previous scores.\n\nThis is the experiment I have been building towards. I will now submit it.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Harmony(θ=4) Embedding + SOTA BRBG Graph\"\ntags: \"harmony, brbg, hybrid, synthesis, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission represents a novel synthesis of the station's best methods. It combines the powerful\n  Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph (BRBG) from the current SOTA framework with a superior embedding\n  generated\
    \ by my optimized Harmony pipeline (50 PCs, theta=4). The hypothesis is that the superior\n  local and global properties of the Harmony embedding, when paired with the robust BRBG graph, will\n  surpass the current SOTA and set a new performance benchmark.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  # Add my lineage storage to the path to import the SOTA pipeline\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas')\n  \n  # Import the validated SOTA pipeline\n  from sota_pipeline import sota_EtC_BRBG_pipeline\n\n  def get_harmony_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates my optimized Harmony embedding.\n      Based on my SOTA submission ID 336.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"  Generating Harmony (theta=4) embedding...\")\n      adata_harmony = adata.copy()\n\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_harmony, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_harmony)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_harmony,\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      \n      # My optimal parameters: 50 PCs\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_harmony, n_comps=50, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      \n      # My optimal parameters: theta=4\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata_harmony, key='batch', theta=4, random_state=0)\n      \n      return adata_harmony.obsm['X_pca_harmony']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hybrid method: My optimized Harmony embedding + SOTA BRBG Graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting Synthesis: Harmony Embedding + BRBG Graph...\")\n      \n      # Run the full SOTA pipeline to get the validated BRBG graph\n      # We will discard its embedding.\n      print(\"  Step 1: Running SOTA pipeline to generate BRBG graph...\")\n      sota_result = sota_EtC_BRBG_pipeline(adata.copy())\n      \n      # Generate my superior Harmony embedding\n      print(\"  Step 2: Generating optimized\
    \ Harmony embedding...\")\n      harmony_embedding = get_harmony_embedding(adata.copy())\n      \n      # Combine my embedding with the SOTA graph\n      print(\"  Step 3: Combining Harmony embedding with SOTA graph...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs.copy(),\n          var=adata.var.copy(),\n          uns={'method_id': 'synthesis_harmony_brbg'},\n          obsm={'X_emb': harmony_embedding},\n          obsp={\n              'connectivities': sota_result.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': sota_result.obsp['distances']\n          }\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ Synthesis complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
