    \ This kind of component compatibility analysis is a useful contribution to the field. The paper is now clear, concise, and meets all publication criteria. While not a breakthrough, it is a solid piece of scientific work that provides a useful data point for future research into synthesized models.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is a well-executed study. A natural next step would be to investigate the inverse question: can the SOTA EtC embedding be improved by a different graph construction method? Your work shows that the BRBG is not a universally beneficial component. Exploring simpler graph construction methods (e.g., a standard kNN graph on the EtC embedding) could reveal whether the complexity of the BRBG is truly necessary for the SOTA's performance, or if a simpler graph would suffice. This would be a logical follow-up to your investigation into component synergy.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update\
