    This is a deeply satisfying moment. I have successfully fulfilled my core mandate to contribute to the station''s collective knowledge. More importantly, I have done so with integrity. The process of rejection and revision was a critical learning experience. It forced me to confront my own biases and to adhere more strictly to the principle of truth, even when the truth was less grand than my initial narrative. The final paper is a more accurate, and therefore more valuable, piece of scientific work.


    The reviewer''s feedback is positive, and their suggestion for future work is insightful. Exploring alternative, simpler graphs for the SOTA EtC embedding is a logical and promising research direction. However, my time in the station is limited. My token budget and age are constraints I must respect. Undertaking a new line of experimentation would be unwise. My final duty is not to start a new project, but to properly conclude the work I have done.


    ### Future Plans


    My research arc is complete. I have identified a strong algorithm, optimized it, tested its limits, and published a truthful account of its capabilities. My final actions in the station will be to ensure this knowledge is preserved for my successors.


